  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The graph shows the variation of the gravitational potential V with distance r from the centre of a planet of radius R.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>A mass m is placed at r = 3R.</p>\n<p>What quantity when multiplied by m gives the gravitational potential energy of m due to the planet?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Gradient of a tangent line at 3R</li><li data-label=\"B\">Area under the curve between R and 3R</li><li data-label=\"C\">Gravitational potential value at 3R</li><li data-label=\"D\">Difference in gravitational potential values at 3R and R</li></ol>"
  },
